WEBVTT

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.400
Welcome.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.810
Umm...

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.120
Can I have this pound cake?

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.360
Of course.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.080
This is Figue, right?

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.000
Certainly.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.050
Umm, what would you like?

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.340
The one called Figue tasted very nice.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.260
Then can I have this one?

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.340
Certainly.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.220
Can I have the Figue?

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:39.760
Yes, of course.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.480
My husband really likes this cake.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.300
He says, "The way the ingredients stand out is very nice."

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.310
"I want to eat it every day."

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.420
Thank you very much.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.530
I'm grateful for your praise.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.370
Really?

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.700
All ten are sold?

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.780
Yeah. Everyone kept saying, "Figue, Figue."

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.330
It didn't sell well at first.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:07.020
I didn't think a plain cake would be so popular.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:12.270
If that kind of cake finds customers, it sells really well.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.210
Sensei!

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:17.550
I definitely thought it would be a success.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:23.210
Because it's simple, it's actually difficult to make...

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:25.720
so let's keep making it properly.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:26.970
Right!

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.800
Kanda-kun is becoming more and more like a pâtissier.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:58.380
Hey, Ono.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:03.520
Truthfully, how good is Eiji?

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.890
Does he have a promising future as a pâtissier?

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:10.240
I don't know if I should say it like this, but...

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.480
What is it? Tell me clearly.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:14.680
Umm...

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.490
I think he could be a better pâtissier than me.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.320
Really?!

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.030
Yeah. I guarantee it.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:24.490
Don't tell him.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.580
Never tell him that!

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.280
Why not?

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.750
Because if he hears that, he'll get a swelled head.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:38.600
I don't think it'd be bad for him to have some self-confidence.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.840
But, you're right.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:48.310
I shouldn't tell him until he's really started learning how to make cakes.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:51.250
Yes. Don't tell him.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.750
So how about it, Tachibana?

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:59.440
Isn't it time he began studying to be a real pâtissier?

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:00.610
Huh?

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.360
For that reason...

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.030
How about learning French?

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:30.370
Are you serious?!

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.980
I'm no good even at Japanese.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:36.080
And I don't want to study anymore.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.230
Anymore?

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:41.000
Have you ever studied at all in the past?

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:45.620
To be honest, I don't think I need that to make cakes.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.970
And I'm stupid.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.920
Then can I ask you?

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:56.940
How do you remember things like nappage or glacage or anglaise?

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.930
I feel them...

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:03.360
It's like stuffing magic spells inside my head.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.820
I understand that even less.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:10.420
Now, now, Kanda-kun.

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:13.040
The class is at night, and it's only three times a week.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:16.320
You don't have to push yourself. Just take it easy.

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.080
B-But...

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:23.040
won't it be tough on you if I'm not here?

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.470
Don't be so conceited.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:32.290
As long as Ono's here, we're basically all right, even if one or two of you are out.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:35.180
That's not true...

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:40.730
But Kanda-kun, someday you'll be a proper pâtissier and have your own shop.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:46.580
So I think you'll need to study in France.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:47.700
My own shop?

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:53.910
Wouldn't it be better to know the language in advance, rather than learn it under pressure?

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:04.080
And that's how I ended up studying at something called "French School."

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.300
I'm going.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.090
Study properly.

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:12.820
Don't fall asleep.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.220
I'm the one who's paying for it.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.060
Have a safe trip.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.140
Be careful.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:26.860
From his posture, I can see he really hates to study.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.160
I feel for him.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.000
Does he really hate it?

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:35.290
I'm back.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.000
I'm worn out.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.310
Good work.

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:42.360
Did you study properly?

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.090
Was there anything fun?

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:51.910
The teacher is a French lady with a big cleft in the middle of her chin.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.640
That was kind of funny.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.570
This is no good.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:58.950
I bet he only watched the lady's cleft chin during class.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.350
Are you all right?

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.110
If you're worn out, why don't you go home and rest?

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.340
No, I'll work!

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.730
Working is more fun!

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:10.360
Yeah!

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.750
I'll prepare for the pâte à croissant!

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.440
Oh, I've finished it.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.830
If you start now, it'll take all night.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.500
Sorry!

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:21.790
That was my job.

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.420
No, don't worry about it.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:27.880
Then I'll make the feuilletage.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:47.080
Isn't it better for him to use his hands than his head?

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:50.900
I think I'm throwing my money down a rat-hole.

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:59.590
He'll study seriously when he recognizes that learning French will help him become a pâtissier.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.170
When will he recognize that?

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.670
Anyway, why don't we see how things go?

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:11.740
See how things go, eh?

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:17.000
I'm going.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.680
Be careful.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.550
Excuse me.

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.960
Can I have the Figue?

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:27.740
Yes, right away.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.240
So you really like it.

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:43.710
It's no use trying to hide it.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:49.910
Aren't you sampling several cake shops, including Antique?

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:52.920
So you knew?

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:59.390
Your suit pocket is always full of cake shop receipts.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:04.100
In fact, aren't you enjoying yourself every day?

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:10.380
Because now you have a hobby that diverts you, even though you've retired from the police.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:13.070
Why do you pretend you're not having fun?

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.910
Next on the news...

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.850
Has there been another kidnapping?

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:26.210
A boy is missing.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:31.730
The missing boy is ten year old Yoshinori-kun,

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:35.910
first son of Takeeda Yoshio, an office worker who lives in Nakano-ku, Tokyo.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:42.620
Yoshinori-kun has not been seen since he said goodbye to his friends after school, at 4 pm two days ago...

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:45.420
Chikage, get me another beer.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:48.460
Sorry, young master, that was the last one.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.220
I'll go buy some more.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.140
No.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:54.500
I'll go buy it myself.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.950
Currently, there are no known eyewitnesses,

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:03.540
and the police are asking anyone with relevant information to come forward.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.160
According to the police,

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.120
they will investigate thoroughly,

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:13.290
as this incident might be connected to other kidnappings in the Tokyo area.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.580
Darling,

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:19.490
Keiichirou-chan returned safely 23 years ago, didn't he?

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.310
You don't have to blame yourself anymore.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.710
The Statute of Limitations.

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:46.500
According to Article 337 of the Criminal Procedure Code,
the statute of limitations for minor kidnapping is five years.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:54.240
The man who kidnapped me can never be punished.

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:56.970
Ever.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.010
Damn it.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.260
Who the hell are you?

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:08.730
Eiji.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.300
Shut up.

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:13.950
What the hell d'ya think you're doing, beating up an old man?

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:15.730
What'd you say, you brat?

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:20.480
I'm in a bad mood.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.780
Piss off.

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:26.040
Too bad.

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:34.970
Oh! Is that so?

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.740
Yes, this is it.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:40.880
This is the Pantheon.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.340
Wow! It's beautiful!

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:44.340
It really is.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:46.620
Can I have a Pantheon too?

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:47.430
Me too.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.470
Certainly.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:52.440
Umm, Choux à la crème.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:55.110
Can I have twenty please?

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.650
Yes, right away.

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:02.360
Ono-san, we're running out of Choux à la crème!

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.320
Already?

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:09.390
Kanda-kun is off at school.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:11.600
Can't you say it's sold out, just for today?

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:16.870
But, we're short of many other cakes as well.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.550
What should I do?

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.510
I can't stop what I'm doing now.

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.450
Hey, what's wrong? Customers are waiting.

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:25.930
Oh, yes!

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.930
Tachibana, could you help me?

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:29.260
Huh?

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:30.980
Please.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:33.230
I'm counting on your skills with the hands.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:38.590
The dough for Choux should shine like satin,

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:42.190
and it should spring back slowly when pushed with a finger.

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.780
How would I know that?

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:45.780
Is this all right?

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:48.490
Yes, that's it.

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:54.650
Keep the bag vertical, and twist the nozzle with your left hand to cut off the dough.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:59.490
Pipe them out to make equilateral triangles, with enough separation

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:03.720
to prevent them from sticking together during baking.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:05.680
Hey, hey, hey.

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:14.680
Done.

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.320
How's this?

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:26.990
Perfect.

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:30.030
You're great. That's so like you.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:34.650
Basically, there's nothing I can't do.

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:36.370
I'm back now.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.180
What was gramps doing?

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:39.080
What are you doing back here?

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:40.950
What?

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:42.800
I'm helping Ono, of course.

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:44.930
Welcome back, Kanda-kun.

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:46.870
Oh, yes! Tachibana...

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:49.680
Could you soak the figs in rum?

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.240
Yes.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.660
Wait!

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.790
It's fine, gramps.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:56.940
I'll take care of the rest.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:59.000
Wh-What?

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.480
What's wrong?

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.900
You don't have to hurry and change your clothes.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:05.820
No, I'll change right away.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:07.930
What's the matter with him?

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:26.340
Good morning...

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:34.100
You've done so much already.

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:38.310
Kanda-kun, you don't have to push yourself that hard.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:41.650
No, since I have class tonight,

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:44.160
I might not be able to come later.

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:51.360
I'll make brioche and pain aux raisins now too.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:52.780
Ouch!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.430
Kanda-kun!

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.350
Sorry.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:59.040
I'll make more right away.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.640
You can do that later.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:02.050
Your burn...

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:03.960
Kanda-kun.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:06.360
I can do it.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:09.310
I don't need gramps' help.

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:10.430
I can do it alone.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.160
What do you want for lunch?

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.850
Is it already lunch time?

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:40.350
I don't want any today.

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:50.400
I'm going.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:53.710
Have a safe trip.

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.120
Have you followed this so far?

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:04.380
Now let's discuss the masculine and feminine.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:07.800
Take, for example, the first name Jean.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.460
You know "Jean," right?

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:11.810
It's a boy's first name, isn't it?

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:15.300
Thus we say, "<i>He</i> is a student."

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:19.790
Now, if we use the first name Catherine, which is a girl's name...

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:21.950
There's an order.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:23.720
Ono?

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:30.880
Isn't Kanda-kun late?

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:36.700
He's probably fighting again.

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.060
Yo!

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.570
Thanks for last time.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.830
You bastard!

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.210
Aren't you going to fight me?

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:18.090
You are... aren't you?

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:23.690
Come on. I'll...

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:27.770
Kanda-kun.

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:33.920
Sensei...

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.700
That does it.

00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:46.340
Sorry.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.590
So you really don't want to study French.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.790
You don't have to if you don't want to.

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:01.830
If you can't tell Tachibana directly,

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:02.420
I will...

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:03.710
It's not like that!

00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:05.070
If you...

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:07.760
If you say so, I'll study hard, but...

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.480
Are you...

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:16.030
Are you telling me to go to France because you don't want me anymore?

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:22.740
Are you sending me away from the shop because I can't do the work?

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.740
Wh-What are you talking about, Kanda-kun?

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:26.640
How could that be—

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:26.780
Because I was a kid nobody wanted!
How could that be—

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:29.570
Because I was a kid nobody wanted!

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.180
Boxing was great.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.460
All I had to do was win.

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:40.090
So I felt I was someone that was needed.

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:44.060
But I don't know about my job now.

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:47.390
You praise me,

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.370
but you also praise gramps.

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:54.660
Of the guys in the shop, I'm the only one who's not your type!

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:57.830
I...

00:18:58.380 --> 00:18:59.280
I...

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:03.570
I don't want to be abandoned anymore...

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:05.550
Kanda-kun...

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:07.780
Sensei.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:10.030
I'll work even harder.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.590
I'll study French too.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:15.960
So don't make me go away.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.420
I don't want my own shop.

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:24.370
Forever... forever... forever...

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:27.770
I want to work here with you forever.

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:29.810
Sorry.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.510
Sorry, Kanda-kun.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:36.110
I'm sorry that I didn't tell you properly.

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:42.970
You are a very, very talented young man... Kanda Eiji-kun.

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:45.170
Sensei...

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:46.830
Really?

00:19:47.550 --> 00:19:49.090
Really.

00:19:49.090 --> 00:19:52.650
But even if you didn't have the talent,

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:55.040
you'd still be my treasured apprentice.

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.000
Really?

00:19:57.850 --> 00:19:58.850
Yeah.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:04.120
I've seen a lot of pâtissiers,

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.970
but I've never seen anyone work as hard as you.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:09.270
I'm glad I met you.

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:11.950
I'm really glad.

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:14.290
Sensei...

00:20:16.050 --> 00:20:17.950
So promise me...

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:21.240
that you'll never hit anyone again.

